// Line editing for a terminal REPL, bound to linenoise.
//
// There is no `dependencies` block because linenoise depends on nothing but the C library and the
// POSIX terminal interface named below.
//
// This is the block a *consumer* writes to reach this package, and resolution for it is built
// (`design/packages.md` §§ 3-6): a `sysl build` fetches the coordinate, selects by MVS, checks what
// arrived against `sysl.sum`, and compiles it as more modules.
//
//     dependencies {
//       linenoise { git = "github.com/sysl-lang/linenoise", version = "0.2.1" }
//     }
//
// The coordinate is identity rather than a URL, so it carries no `https://`, and the version is the
// tag `v0.2.1` on this repository. `build-lib` and `--lib` still work, but they are no longer the
// only way in.

package {
  name    = "linenoise"
  version = "0.2.1"
}

// A terminal is the operating system's, and so is the file the history is saved to. linenoise also
// needs `posix` outright: it puts the terminal into raw mode with `tcsetattr` and asks its size with
// `ioctl`, neither of which is C's standard library.
//
// Saying so here is what turns "this cannot work on a freestanding target" into one refusal before
// anything is compiled, rather than a link error naming a symbol.
requires {
  posix = true
}
